neutrino-mass-right-handed-neutrino-mass.interpretation:
The relation connects the observed light neutrino mass scale $m_{
u} \sim 0.1	ext{ eV}$ to the right-handed singlet Majorana mass scale $M_R \sim 10^{14}	ext{ GeV}$. Setting the Dirac mass scale $m_D \sim y_{
u} v$ to the electroweak scale ($v \approx 246	ext{ GeV}$ with $\mathcal{O}(1)$ Yukawa coupling $y_{
u} \sim 1$) leads directly to $M_R \approx m_D^2 / m_{
u} \approx (100	ext{ GeV})^2 / (0.1	ext{ eV}) \approx 10^{14}	ext{ GeV}$, naturally placing new lepton-number-violating physics near the Grand Unified Theory (GUT) energy regime.
